+# My Discord Gacha Bot
+
+A Python `discord.py` gacha / party-battle bot with hero pulls, character progression, a food lab, story battles, admin tools, and generated card art.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- Python **3.10+**
+- A Discord application and bot token from the [Discord Developer Portal](https://discord.com/developers/applications)
+
+## Local setup
+
+```bash
+# Clone the repository, then enter it
+cd My-discord-bot
+
+# Optional but recommended: create and activate a virtual environment
+python -m venv .venv
+# Windows PowerShell: .venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
+# macOS/Linux: source .venv/bin/activate
+
+# Install the bot dependencies
+python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
+
+# Create your local secrets file from the safe template
+# Windows PowerShell: Copy-Item .env.example .env
+# macOS/Linux: cp .env.example .env
+```
+
+Edit `.env` and add the values below:
+
+```dotenv
+DISCORD_TOKEN=your_real_bot_token_here
+OWNER_ID=your_discord_user_id
+# Optional: shows slash-command changes immediately in this test server
+GUILD_ID=your_test_server_id
+```
+
+> **Never commit or share `.env`, a bot token, API key, or a live player database.** If a Discord token is ever exposed, reset it in **Discord Developer Portal → Bot → Reset Token** immediately.
+
+In the Discord Developer Portal, enable the bot's **Message Content Intent** and **Server Members Intent**, then start it:
+
+```bash
+python bot.py
+```
+
+## Useful commands
+
+- `/pull` — summon heroes
+- `/heroes`, `/book`, `/profile`, `/inventory` — view progression
+- `/party view`, `/party set`, `/party clear` — manage the battle team
+- `/level` — play story chapters and battles
+- `/lab` — convert heroes to food and upgrade food
+- `/shop`, `/daily` — economy and daily tasks
+- `/admin ...` — owner-only administration commands; requires `OWNER_ID`
+
+## Content files
+
+- `heroes.csv` — hero roster, stats, skills, banners, and cooldowns
+- `story_chapters.csv` — story and chapter enemy/reward data
+- `Assets/` — card art, full art, banners, avatars, icons, and story images
+- `config.py` — shared battle and progression tuning values
+
+The bot synchronizes CSV-authored heroes and story chapters to the local SQLite database on startup.
+
+## Testing
+
+Run the regression tests with:
+
+```bash
+python -m unittest discover -s tests -v
+```
+
+For balance experimentation, `balance_tune.py` runs simulations against a throwaway database and writes `heroes_tuned.csv`; review that output before replacing `heroes.csv`.
+
+## Data and Git safety
+
+`gacha.db` is the live local SQLite database. It contains player IDs, display names, inventory, party, and progression, so it must stay local. It is ignored by `.gitignore` for new Git commits; do not upload it manually through the GitHub website either.
